          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong displayed category
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the “classifying map” of a category over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            and a functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:D\to C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            over it. The operation (which is an
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:D\to C
            is a generalization of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-Grothendieck+construction"} T-Grothendieck construction
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the theory of categories.
          %p
            Displayed categories are particularly useful in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
            (especially
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories+in+homotopy+type+theory"} internal categories in homotopy type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : D \to C
            for which preservation of identity and composition is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definitional+equality"} definitional equality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strictification"} strictification
            of functors.
          %p
            Displayed categories are also useful philosophically to preserve the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity-on-objects"} identity-on-objects
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibrations"} Grothendieck fibrations
            and strict
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/creation+of+limits"} creation of limits
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:D\to C
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#by_components By components
          %p
            A
            %strong displayed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            over a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            consists of
          %ul
            %li
              for each object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(a)
            %li
              for each object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:C
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b:C
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi a
                      %mo →
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:a \to b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:D(a)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:D(b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi f
