                %path{:d => "M -2.487281 2.869844 C -2.032715 1.145916 -1.017939 0.334934 -0.000426862 0.00140084 C -1.019597 -0.333099 -2.032861 -1.146278 -2.487767 -2.867675 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(-0.82307,0.56924,0.56924,0.82307,77.47932,43.59284)"}
                %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                  %use{:x => "93.943", "xlink:href" => "#THRp8dLSOWx5QTW90uqrBSgkIx8=-glyph2-1", :y => "40.396"}
                %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                  %use{:x => "98.806", "xlink:href" => "#THRp8dLSOWx5QTW90uqrBSgkIx8=-glyph3-2", :y => "41.736"}
                %path{:d => "M -37.673844 16.360812 L 37.166 16.360812 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:miter;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(1,0,0,-1,67.334,30.603)"}
                %path{:d => "M -2.485654 2.870186 C -2.032529 1.14753 -1.02081 0.33503 -0.00127875 -0.0009075 C -1.02081 -0.332939 -2.032529 -1.149345 -2.485654 -2.868095 ", :style => "fill:none;stroke-width:0.47818;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke:rgb(0%,0%,0%);stroke-opacity:1;stroke-miterlimit:10;", :transform => "matrix(1,0,0,-1,104.73956,14.24128)"}
                %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                  %use{:x => "61.274", "xlink:href" => "#THRp8dLSOWx5QTW90uqrBSgkIx8=-glyph4-1", :y => "2.573"}
                %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                  %use{:x => "68.331", "xlink:href" => "#THRp8dLSOWx5QTW90uqrBSgkIx8=-glyph2-2", :y => "8.994"}
          %p
            The crucial thing to notice here is that, fundamentally, such a functor over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is defined ‘fiberwise’, in the sense that, choosen an object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \phi
            has to restrict to a functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi x
                    %mo :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mi G
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int\phi_x : \pi_F^{-1}x \to \pi_G^{-1}x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Fx
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fx
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gx
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gx
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \phi_x
            can be naturally defined to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_x
            itself.
          %p
            Now what’s left to define is the action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \phi
            on those arrows that cross fibers (in a sense, all the arrows except those that map to identities in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            – or, put differently again, the above discussion pinned down the object part of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \phi
          %p
            Thus let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo ♯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,f^\sharp):(x,x') \to (y,y')
            be a morphism in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,x')
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y,y')
            using
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_y
            respectively, so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo ♯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \phi(f,f^\sharp)
            has to be an arrow
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,\phi_x(x')) \to (y,\phi_y(y'))
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} st
                      %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{st}^{\phi}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} st
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ′
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Gf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{st}^{\phi}_{x',y'} : Ff(x',y') \to Gf(\phi_x(x'),\phi_y(y'))
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \phi
          %p
            Functoriality of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \phi
            is a direct consequence of the properties required to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+natural+transformation"} vertical natural transformation
          %h2#properties_of_functors_through_properties_of_the_reindexing Properties of functors through properties of the reindexing
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:E \to B
            be a functor, call
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dF
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dF : B^{op} \to Prof
            the associated lax normal functor. By requiring a different degree of laxity to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dF
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dF
            or which subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prof
            it hits, we can express different properties of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %ol
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dF
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dF
              is a pseudofunctor, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conduch%C3%A9+fibration"} Conduché fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dF
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dF
              factors through the inclusion
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo →
                      %mi Prof
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat \to Prof
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prefibration"} prefibration
            %li
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dF
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dF
              is both Conduché and a prefibration, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            %li
              Call
              %em partial functor
              a profunctor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : X \to Psh(Y)
              that factors through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi Psh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y,0) : Y + 1 \to Psh(Y)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              and picks the empty presheaf otherwise. When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dF
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dF
              factors through the subcategory of partial functors it is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foliated+category"} foliation
          %p
            These and more examples are discussed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Benabou"} Benabou
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The correspondence between categories over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+lax+functors"} normal lax functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to Prof
            was observed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Benabou"} Bénabou
            already in 1972:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Benabou"}> Jean Bénabou
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em 2-dimensional limits and colimits of distributors (or how to glue together categories)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oberwolfach"} Oberwolfach
              ‘Tagungsbericht’, 1972,
              %a{:href => "https://oda.mfo.de/handle/mfo/1575"} (web)
          %p A more detailed account of Benabou’s work on this topic can be found at:
          %ul
            %li#Benabou
              %p
                Jean Bénabou,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Distributors at work
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/FIBR/DiWo.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  Graham Manuell
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Graham+Manuell"} ?
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monoid extensions and the Grothendieck construction
                %strong 105
                (2022) 488–507 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00233-022-10294-2"}> doi:10.1007/s00233-022-10294-2
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p The term “displayed category”, and the applications to type theory, are due to:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benedikt+Ahrens"}> Benedikt Ahrens
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"} Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
              = succeed "," do
                %em Displayed Categories
              %strong 15
              1, (2019) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.23638/LMCS-15(1:20)2019"}> doi:10.23638/LMCS-15(1:20)2019
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.04296"} arXiv:1705.04296
          %p
            An unpacking of the definition as lax functors into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Span"} Span
            is in 2.2 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Du%C5%A1ko+Pavlovi%C4%87"}> Duško Pavlović
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samson+Abramsky"} Samson Abramsky
              = succeed "," do
                %em Specifying Interaction Categories
              %strong 1290
              (1997) 147–158. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0026986"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0026986
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Also cited above:
          %ul
            %li#CS
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geoff+Cruttwell"}> Geoff Cruttwell
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike Shulman
              = succeed "," do
                %em A unified framework for generalized multicategories
              %strong 24
              21 (2010) 580-655. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/24/21/24-21abs.html"}> TAC
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
